# nr-office-engine-render: the render action of the office engine (module mixdog-office::render)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (rustfmt parsed every file; the twin test replays a recording made by running the recorder
against C:/Project/mixdog). The module is a library the Office tool's service (a later task of the office track) calls; this task registers no
protocol method and no service, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

It needs these wires applied first (they add what this module calls): nr-office-pdf-render-pages.wire (mixdog_office_pdf::render; already in lib.rs
of the tree), nr-office-ooxml-xlsx-operations.wire (mixdog_ooxml::xlsx and ::xlsx_recalculate), nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire (the manifest lines
below overlap with it: see Cargo.toml).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod session;` add (and extend the crate doc by one line: "[`render`] draws a session's document: the export to a PDF, the page images,
the review token, the whole-result cache and the page-by-page reuse of a deck."):

    pub mod render;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], after `mixdog-fsio`/`mixdog-js` (keeping the list sorted). `mixdog-office-com`, `mixdog-office-pdf`, `mixdog-office-quality` and
`mixdog-ooxml` are the lines nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire already adds: add each once. New with this task:

    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-author = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt"] }

(`mixdog-fonts` is a [dev-dependencies] line in nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire: make it a [dependencies] line instead; nothing of mixdog-office-author,
-pdf, -quality, -com or mixdog-ooxml depends on mixdog-office, so there is no cycle. `tokio` is also already a [dev-dependencies] line (feature rt):
keep both. All are [workspace.dependencies] entries and members already; no external crate enters the lock.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock
Package `mixdog-office`: add the dependencies mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-author (and the ones nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire names), tokio
(`cargo update -w` offline).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing by hand: no new external crate, no new feature. Run the hakari check after the manifest edit and take its output if it asks for a line.

