## Interface the tool layer calls (crate mixdog-office, `mixdog_office::render`)

- `render(&E, &P, &SessionHandle, args: &Value, cwd: &Path, &dyn Receipts) -> Result<Value, String>` (async) is `render(session, args, cwd)` of
  office-actions-render.mjs: the portable workbook calculated first, the preview, and for a deck (or a PDF of designed pages) the receipt and contact sheet
  through `mixdog_office_author::review_artifacts::pptx_review_artifacts`. `E: RenderEngine`, `P: WriteProof` writes the contact sheet; `Receipts` is the
  seam of the author crate (the receipt functions belong to the engine task that owns the snapshot).
- `render::preview::render_office_preview(&E, &SessionHandle, &Value, &Path, PreviewOptions { reuse_latest })` and `cached_office_preview(&E, &SessionHandle,
  &Value, &Path, reuse_latest) -> Result<Option<Value>, String>` are `renderOfficePreview` / `cachedOfficePreview`: what qa and finalize call
  (`acquireQaPreview`, the finalize reuse). The result is Node's object (`_images` with the pixels, `images` without, key order kept).
- `render::recalculate_for_review(&E, &SessionHandle)` is `recalculateForReview` (qa and finalize call it as well).
- `render::SystemRender::new(LaneTokens, OfficeCom, Arc<Registry>, Arc<dyn WriteNote>)` is the engine of a process: files on the lanes, LibreOffice through
  `Soffice::process()` (a portable Word document is drawn twice so its contents field learns its page numbers from the PDF layout), Microsoft Office
  through `OfficeCom::call` (300 s), pages through `mixdog_office_pdf::render::render_pdf_pages`, the recalculation through
  `mixdog_ooxml::xlsx_recalculate::recalculate_portable_workbook` with the call's cancellation followed by a watcher, the autofit refit through
  `apply_xlsx`. The `WriteNote` is the call's write ledger.
- `render::page_cache`: `pptx_page_signatures`, `reusable_pptx_pages`, `complete_page_coverage`; `render::toc_pages::number_docx_table_of_contents`.
- What a session must hold for the whole-result cache: an owned, not visible, not attached session (`session.com.ownership == Some("owned")`,
  `com.visible != Some(true)`, mode not Visible or Attach). The open/create task sets `com.ownership = Some("owned")` and `visible = Some(false)` on every
  portable session, as Node's `extra: { ownership: 'owned', visible: false }` does; the snapshot module reads the same fields.
- The caches live on the session as Node's objects (`caches.render`, `caches.page_render`, `caches.preview_export_key`, `design_state.rendered_*`).

## Not in this task / left for another
- `applyPortableOoxmlBatch` (portable-ooxml.mjs, nr-office-engine-open-create) is not in the tree yet: the refit of a recalculated workbook's autofit
  ranges (`RenderEngine::refit_columns`) is written directly as `load_package` + `apply_xlsx` + `save_package` in `SystemRender`; for an xlsx batch that
  is all `applyPortableOoxmlBatch` does (the orphan-part removal and the contents refresh are for deck and Word operations). When that task lands it may
  point `refit_columns` at its own front.
- The finalize test of office-render-preview.test.mjs (`finalize uses a complete custom preview and still validates the saved deck`) runs the author,
  finalize and session actions: it belongs to the finalize task. The set_text / stable-ID / hidden-Word-run / hidden-slide audit tests of
  pptx-incremental.test.mjs run the batch, snapshot and issues actions: they belong to those tasks; the signature and incremental-render tests are
  ported in tests/twin_render.rs.

## What was not compiled or run
Nothing was compiled or run in Rust. The first compile of the module and of tests/twin_render.rs is the lead's. `twin_live_render` (ignored) re-records
through Node and LibreOffice on the migration PC and was not run.
